    "sceneBrief": "Rainsford slides down from the tree after Zaroff's retreat, sick with the knowledge that he is being saved for another day's sport. He forces himself to think. Three hundred yards from his hiding place, he finds a huge dead tree leaning precariously on a smaller living one. He works frantically with his knife, constructing a Malay man-catcher — a trap that will drop the dead tree on anyone who trips its trigger. He hides behind a fallen log and waits. Zaroff returns, tracking with bloodhound precision. He steps on the trigger bough and senses danger at the last instant, leaping back — but the dead tree still strikes him a glancing blow on the shoulder. Zaroff laughs, congratulates Rainsford, and retreats to dress his wound.",
